{% from 'ingressroute.yml.j2' import monitoring_route with context %}
---
{# daniel-pi's promtail push door, and deliberately NOT an entry on the route next door.

   THE MARKER THIS ANSWERS: the `# DECIDED 2026-08-24` block in ingressroute.yaml.j2 narrowed
   that route from PathPrefix(`/`) + the whole pod CIDR to `/loki/api/v1/` + the two node
   gateways, after verifying live that the old pair gave every pod read, forged-write and delete
   on an `auth_enabled: false` Loki. Its stated residual is that `/loki/api/v1/` still contains
   push and delete, "now reachable only from the two nodes rather than from any pod".

   The Pi needs push. Adding 10.0.0.139/32 to that route's extra_client_cidrs would have been the
   one-line change — and it would have handed the Pi delete and full query as well, walking back
   the residual that block was careful to bound. So this is a SEPARATE router with a longer
   prefix and its own client list: the Pi gets `/loki/api/v1/push` and nothing else, and the two
   nodes' query access is untouched. The marker is extended, not contradicted.

   Ordering does not decide this. Both routers sit at priority 100, but the route next door
   cannot match Pi traffic at all — its ClientIP clause does not list the Pi — so Traefik skips
   it and this router is the only candidate. No priority juggling to get wrong.

   `k8s_bridge_client_ip` (daniel-server) rides along because the macro always prepends it. That
   grants nothing new: daniel-server already reaches `/loki/api/v1/` on the other route, and this
   prefix is a subset of it.

   Push is a WRITE on an unauthenticated store, so state what this trusts: one host we own, on
   the LAN, identified by source address. If Loki ever gains real authentication, this whole
   route should go and the Pi should carry a credential instead. #}
{{ monitoring_route(
    container_item.name ~ '-push',
    container_item.hostname | default(container_item.name),
    container_item.port,
    '/loki/api/v1/push',
    extra_client_cidrs=[k8s_pi_client_ip ~ '/32'],
    service_name=container_item.name
  )
}}
